                <pb facs="0482" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/25876f: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the Soviet Union (Henderson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-09T18:00:00-04:00">December 9, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>620. Your 482, November 20, 11 p.m., from Moscow. You are requested to see
                    Molotov and refer to his conversation with you on November 20 in regard to North
                    Africa. Please inform Molotov that a telegram has been sent to General
                    Eisenhower and Murphy in order that they may seek to clarify to Admiral Darlan
                    the attitude of the United States Government. We desire Mr. Molotov to be orally
                    informed of this telegram. It is being simultaneously telegraphed to our Embassy
                    in London in order that the Ambassador may read it to Mr. Churchill. Please read
                    a paraphrase of the following telegram to Mr. Molotov:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of message of December 7 to General Eisenhower and Mr. Murphy,
                    printed on <ref target="#pg472">page 472</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
